    "### Visualizing Numerical Distribution: Histogram"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dfc73a53",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We can visualize the count of their heights with a **Histogram**, which is one type of *Distribution Plot*; named as such because it shows where the values of the variable `height` lie on the x-axis, and how many of them are there (count).\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead of showing all the values, we group them into **Bins** of uniform size, and represent how many values in the bin, vertically, by the height of bin itself.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the simplest and most useful type of statistical plot. In seaborn, it is `displot` (distribution plot), like so:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
