  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cc02226a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Distribution Statistics"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "50f6c250",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We describe a distribtuion by three properties:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Central Tendency**\n",
    "2. **Dispersion**\n",
    "3. **Skewness**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e8a6716e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1. Central Tendency\n",
    "\n",
    " 1. **Mode**: the most frequent value.\n",
    " 2. **Median**: the middle value when data are ordered.\n",
    " 3. **Mean** (average): the center of \"mass\" ($\\bar{x}$ or $\\mu$).\n",
    "\n",
    "The mean ($\\mu$) is the sum of the values divided by their count:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\mu = \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^{N} x_i\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "- $\\mu$ denotes population mean\n",
    "- $N$ is the count"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fa989a0f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2. Dispersion\n",
    "\n",
    "  1. **Range**: the difference between the maximum and minimum values.\n",
    "  2. **Variance**: the average of the squared differences from the mean ($\\sigma^2$).\n",
    "  3. **Standard Deviation**: the square root of the variance ($\\sigma$).\n",
    "\n",
    "The variance ($\\sigma^2$) is described mathematically as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\sigma^2 = \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^{N}(x_i - \\mu)^2\n",
    "$$"
   ]
  },
