   "id": "c748394f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Note the following:\n",
    "\n",
    "- The `std` is the standard deviation\n",
    "- The `50%` percentile is the **median** statistic.\n",
    "- The **range** is shown by the **max** and **min** statistics.\n",
    "- The **mode** is more useful when we are looking at categorical attribute. In our case, the attribute is numerical."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6cfa6955",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Percentiles\n",
    "\n",
    "The **median** is the 50th percentile (`50%`) which means that 50% of the data points are below this value.\n",
    "\n",
    "The `25%` and the `75%` percentiles go by other names:\n",
    "  - the 1st and 3rd quartiles\n",
    "  - the Q1 and Q3\n",
    "  - the lower and upper quartiles"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a89b6ac4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3. Skewness\n",
    "\n",
    "We get skewness when the distribution is **not symmetric**:\n",
    "\n",
    "- The *Mode* is the peak\n",
    "- The *Mean* pulls the curve downwards\n",
    "- The *Median* follows the mean a little bit\n",
    "\n",
    "![Skewness](../../assets/skewness.png){height=480}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bced3ba3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This can be calculated using the `.skew()` method where:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `0` Perfectly Symmetrical (Normal).\n",
    "- `>0` Right-skewed: Long tail on the right side.\n",
    "- `<0` Left-skewed: Long tail on the left side."
   ]
  },
