  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3087573b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**What can we say about the Red distribution of height vs the Blue one?**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "67cfb48a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## The Normal Distribution"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cbd097e1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The **Normal Distribution** (or **Gaussian Distribution**) is a bell-shaped distribution that is symmetric around the mean, with the highest density of data points in the center.\n",
    "\n",
    "Human `height` is one example of such distribution."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "86ba9804",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "![The Normal Distribution](../../assets/normal_distribution.png){height=550}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f6900526",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**The 68-95-99.7 Rule**: In a perfect Gaussian distribution, data is distributed with mathematical precision. This is often called the **Empirical Rule**:\n",
    "\n",
    "| **Distance from Mean**                   | **Percentage of Data Included** |\n",
    "| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n",
    "| Within $1\\sigma$ | **68.2%**                       |\n",
    "| Within $2\\sigma$ | **95.4%**                       |\n",
    "| Within $3\\sigma$ | **99.7%**                       |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "21d49d3e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "To *standardize* the distribution values such that they are comparable and statistically interpretable (e.g., flagging outliers), we calculate the **z-score**:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ z = \\frac{x-\\mu}{\\sigma} $$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "\n",
    "- $\\mu$ is the mean\n",
    "- $\\sigma$ is the standard deviation\n",
    "\n",
    "The z-score is also interpreted as:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. centering around the mean\n",
    "2. adjusting by the standard deviation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e8bd54bb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Let's do it in code:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
<<<<<<< HEAD
   "execution_count": 24,
   "id": "7d155062",
=======
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "045e5eb2",
>>>>>>> 3ec4dfec6532de7f929918719ea54b0d9ee05565
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def z_score(series: pd.Series):\n",
    "    return (series - series.mean()) / series.std()\n",
    "\n",
    "df['h_z'] = z_score(df['h_meters'])"
   ]
  },
