  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3706beef",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Interpreting Distributions\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's go back to our comparison: NBA Players vs General Public in terms of Height."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "814ff8b7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Below are the distributions of height in centimeters across:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Adult women globally (mean of `159cm` and standard deviation of `6cm`)\n",
    "- Adult men globally (mean of `171cm` and standard deviation of `7cm`)\n",
    "- NBA players; a specific subset of adult men (~2300 players who have been part of an NBA team roster between 1996 and 2019)\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's visualize it:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a66958f8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "![Comparative Distribution of NBA Player's Heights and Human Heights. Image Source: https://distributionofthings.com/human-height/](../../assets/nba_comparative_distribution.png)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c38469ad",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "The figure above shows\n",
    "\n",
    "- three **Normal** distributions\n",
    "- with increasing centers (as we go right)\n",
    "- and decreasing dispersino (as we go right)\n",
    "\n",
    "Using statistics we can make **General Statements** like:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. \"men are taller than women\" (on average is implied)\n",
    "2. \"most NBA players are taller than most people\"\n",
    "3. \"most NBA players are men\"\n",
    "4. \"very few women are taller than the shortest NBA players\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Notice that since there are overlaps, we can't give **Definitive Statements** like:\n",
    "\n",
    "- \"All men are ... \" (confirmatory)\n",
    "- \"No Player is ...\" (negation)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ac37293c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpreting Outliers\n",
    "\n",
    "When having outliers in one distribution, that might signal to us that it is, in fact, a member of another distribution. In this case:\n",
    "\n",
    "- a Male with a height of `+192cm` might be an **outlier within Males**, but\n",
    "- that's within the normal distribution of **NBA Players**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "99eac02d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "If you want to read more about human height, its evolution across the world and predictions for the future I encourage you to check out this great [article from Our World in Data](https://ourworldindata.org/human-height)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "53d59edd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
