   "source": [
    "### 3. Skewness\n",
    "\n",
    "We get skewness when the distribution is **not symmetric**:\n",
    "\n",
    "- The *Mode* is the peak\n",
    "- The *Mean* pulls the curve downwards\n",
    "- The *Median* follows the mean a little bit\n",
    "\n",
    "![Skewness](../../assets/skewness.png){height=480}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "90f35625",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This can be calculated using the `.skew()` method where:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `0` Perfectly Symmetrical (Normal).\n",
    "- `>0` Right-skewed: Long tail on the right side.\n",
    "- `<0` Left-skewed: Long tail on the left side."
   ]
  },
